# .NET Core Framework File Upload

## File Upload

The following sections describe how to handle file uploads on your server using .Net Core Framework as a server-side language. For information on the upload workflow refer to the [file upload documentation](https://froala.com/wysiwyg-editor/docs/concepts/file/upload/ "File Upload").

### _Frontend_

1.  On the `head` section include the Editor style.


```
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/froala-editor@latest/css/froala_editor.pkgd.min.css" rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" />
  </head>
```

5.  On the `body` section include the Editor JS files and define the area for the editor.


```
<body>  
  <script type="text/javascript" src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/froala-editor@latest/js/froala_editor.pkgd.min.js"></script>

  <div class="sample">
    <h2>File upload example.</h2>
    <form>
      <textarea id="edit" name="content"></textarea>
    </form>
  </div>
```

9.  Initialize the editor and set the file upload URL


```
  <script>
    new FroalaEditor('#edit', {
      // Set the file upload URL.
      fileUploadURL: '/UploadFiles',
      fileUploadParams: {
        id: 'my_editor'
      }
    })
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```

The full code should look like this:

```
